module

public import Mathlib.RingTheory.AdicCompletion.Algebra
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Noetherian.Defs
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Finiteness.Defs
public import Sheaf.RingTheory.AssociatedGradedRing

/-!
# Degree-zero generators for the associated graded of a completed module

Source: Stacks Project, Cohomology of Schemes, Lemma 087Z,
`lemma-finite-over-rees-algebra`, affine assertion in its proof; Algebra, Lemma 05GG
(blueprint: lem-weil-pbc-completed-module-associated-graded-generators).

We state the explicit representative formulation from the node. The first conjunct says
that `M/IM` is a finite `A/I`-module. The second says that any finite family spanning
`M/IM` over `A/I`, with any lifts to `M`, generates every degree of the associated graded,
with coefficients in `Ideal.associatedGradedPiece I n`, represented in `I^n`. Summing
these formulas over the finite support of a graded element gives generation over
`gr_I(A)`. Conversely, taking the degree `n`
component of a graded expression gives precisely this congruence.
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u v

open scoped BigOperators

namespace AdicCompletion

/-- (blueprint: lem-weil-pbc-completed-module-associated-graded-generators)
Stacks Project, Lemma 087Z, affine assertion in the proof: for a finite module over
`AdicCompletion I A`, the quotient `M/IM` is finite over `A/I`, and its generators in
degree zero generate the associated graded. The first assertion is
`Module.Finite (A ⧸ I) (M ⧸ I • ⊤)`; the second quantifies every finite family `xbar`
spanning `M ⧸ I • ⊤` over `A ⧸ I` and every choice of lifts `x`.

Proof, following the node's five steps:
1. The extended ideal is generated by the image of `I`. Its powers act as `I^n • M`
   after restriction of scalars. Multiplication of representatives induces the graded
   action: changing either representative changes the product by `I^(m+n+1)M`.
2. Noetherianity makes `I` finitely generated. By
   `lem-weil-pbc-adic-completion-mod-ideal` (Stacks 05GG), the completion modulo the
   extended ideal is `A/I`. Thus the images of finitely many completion-module
   generators generate `M/IM` over `A/I`.
3. For any lifts `x`, generation of the quotient says
   `M = image(A^t → M) + IM`, where the map sends `c` to `∑ j, c j • x j`.
   For every ideal `J`, `(J Â)M = J • M`: expand a coefficient of the extended ideal
   as a finite sum of products of an element of `J` and an element of the completion.
4. Apply `lem-weil-pbc-module-graded-lift-mod-ideal-power` to this map and `y ∈ I^nM`.
   It gives a tuple with every coefficient in `I^n` and error in `I^(n+1)M`.
   Negating the error gives the displayed sign; `n = 0` is included.
5. In degree `n`, the congruence gives the sum of the degree `n` coefficient classes
   times the degree-zero generator classes. Every graded element has finite support,
   so adding these expressions gives generation over the associated graded ring
   `def-weil-pbc-associated-graded-ring`. -/
theorem completedModule_associatedGraded_generators
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A] (I : Ideal A)
    (M : Type v) [AddCommGroup M] [Module (AdicCompletion I A) M]
    [Module.Finite (AdicCompletion I A) M] :
    letI : Module A M := Module.compHom M (algebraMap A (AdicCompletion I A))
    Module.Finite (A ⧸ I) (M ⧸ (I • ⊤ : Submodule A M)) ∧
    (∀ (t : ℕ) (xbar : Fin t → M ⧸ (I • ⊤ : Submodule A M)),
      Submodule.span (A ⧸ I) (Set.range xbar) = ⊤ →
      ∀ (x : Fin t → M), (∀ j, Submodule.Quotient.mk (x j) = xbar j) →
      ∀ (n : ℕ) (y : M), y ∈ (I ^ n • (⊤ : Submodule A M)) →
        ∃ (b : Fin t → Ideal.associatedGradedPiece I n)
          (a : Fin t → (I ^ n : Ideal A)),
          (∀ j, b j = Submodule.Quotient.mk (a j)) ∧
          y - ∑ j, (a j : A) • x j ∈ (I ^ (n + 1) • (⊤ : Submodule A M))) := by
  sorry

end AdicCompletion
